{"memo": "\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nALDERMOOR INDUSTRIES \u2014 CFO AUDIT MEMORANDUM\nDate: October 24, 2023\nRE: Procurement Request Audit Summary \u2014 Takumi Controls Component Acquisition (\u20ac480,000)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nFollowing a comprehensive tripartite audit of the \u20ac480,000 procurement request for 200 units of industrial PLC controllers and HMI panels for Aldermoor's filling line production, Financial Control has endorsed the CapEx classification under IAS 16. However, Risk & Compliance has flagged high default risk (credit score 45/100) for this critical-path supplier, and Tax & Treasury has issued a formal hold due to an FX variance of 6.04% exceeding our 5% tolerance threshold. Per Aldermoor\u2019s governance framework, the transaction cannot proceed in its current state.\n\nKEY FINDINGS:\n\u2022 Risk & Compliance: REJECTED \u2014 Vendor cleared on sanctions, but credit score is 45/100 (High Risk) for a critical-path supplier, requiring mandatory credit mitigation (prepayment with bank guarantee) or rejection per our risk threshold (<50).\n\u2022 Tax & Treasury: HOLD FOR TREASURY AUDIT \u2014 Total landed cost calculated at \u20ac586,080.00 (including \u20ac14,880 import duty and \u20ac91,200 import VAT for JP-origin goods), but flagged for an FX rate variance of 6.04% (rate used: 1 EUR = 163.5 JPY vs. live market: 1 EUR = 174.01 JPY).\n\u2022 IFRS Financial Control: APPROVED \u2014 Capitalised as CapEx under IAS 16.7 in GL Account Range 0200\u20130299 (Technical Equipment and Machinery), with a 10-year straight-line depreciation schedule (\u20ac48,000/year). Department Head approval threshold satisfied.\n\nFINAL DECISION: CONDITIONAL HOLD\nReason: Triggered by the Tax & Treasury FX alert (\"HOLD FOR TREASURY AUDIT\") and the Risk & Compliance high-risk credit evaluation. Per Aldermoor's delegation-of-authority matrix, payment release is suspended pending FX rate recalculation and the establishment of credit risk mitigation.\n\nNEXT ACTIONS:\n1. Treasury & Procurement Team \u2014 Recalculate invoice pricing using the live FX rate (1 EUR = 174.01 JPY) and re-evaluate total landed cost; secure updated vendor invoicing. \u2014 Deadline: 3 Business Days\n2. Global Procurement Head & Vendor Management \u2014 Enforce credit risk mitigation: negotiate terms requiring a full prepayment backed by a first-demand bank guarantee, or issue a formal rejection of the vendor. \u2014 Deadline: 5 Business Days\n3. Tax & Customs Department \u2014 Verify supplier-provided preferential origin documentation (Form EUR.1 or Supplier's Declaration) to determine potential duty relief under the EU-Japan EPA before final import clearance. \u2014 Deadline: Prior to Customs Entry / Goods Release\n\nSigned,\nCFO Office \u2014 Aldermoor Industries, Hamburg\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550", "timestamp": "2026-11-24T04:25:38.226993Z", "level": "info", "severity": "INFO", "event": "CFO Synthesis complete"}
